# WHAT EAS BUILD IS ALLOWED TO SEE.
#
# THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR `eas build` UPLOADS. Once it exists,
# .gitignore is not consulted at all, so every line that was keeping a secret
# or a bulk directory out of the tarball is repeated at the bottom. Delete a
# line here and it goes up to the build servers.
#
# The two lines that matter are `android/` and `ios/`.
#
# Those directories are not source. They are generated by `expo prebuild` on
# this Windows machine and then patched by Forge. Uploading them makes EAS
# treat this as a BARE project: it stops running its own prebuild and builds
# the files in the tarball instead. That is what failed build 209 with
#
#   Could not resolve project :react-native-async-storage_async-storage
#     > No matching variant ... - No variants exist.
#
# repeated for async-storage, ml-kit, sentry, safe-area-context and screens —
# every third-party native module in the app, and none of the expo-* ones.
# Those five are linked by paths written on Windows into a Gradle project that
# was then unpacked onto Linux, so the project directories resolved to nothing
# and Gradle built five empty shells. The same upload also explains the two
# lines above the failure that should never appear in a cloud build:
#
#   Forge: FORGE_STORE_FILE is not set - release artifacts will be UNSIGNED.
#   sdk.dir property in local.properties file. Problem: Directory does not exist
#
# Forge's signing patch and a `local.properties` pointing at an Android SDK on
# the C: drive, both shipped to a machine where neither exists.
#
# It is also the whole of the 808 MB archive — android/build and android/.gradle
# are hundreds of megabytes of compiled output that get thrown away and rebuilt.
#
# Keep prebuild local for Forge, and let EAS do its own on Linux. It autolinks
# every module correctly because it generates the paths on the machine that
# will use them.
android/
ios/

# --- carried over from .gitignore; see the note at the top ---
node_modules
.expo
dist
*.log
.DS_Store
play-service-account.json
expo-env.d.ts
_*.ps1
_msg.txt
.claude-flow/
.claude/
.env
credentials.json
*.jks
*.keystore
